From 239aade2fb15bb111e0d2fce4cbf81ff997850da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ayiejosh <132535860+ayiejosh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 10:08:35 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 174/269] gallium/pvr: fix two off-by-one-dword errors in the
 static stream placement

The builder now agrees with itself: 368 bytes returned, 368 summed by its own macros, EOT at byte 364.

Round 78's apparent "one inconsistent expression" was two independent errors with one shared cause: the
offset helper returns WHERE the EOT packet is packed, not the end of the stream.
  1. total_dwords omitted the EOT packet's own length, so the builder returned one dword less than its
     macros summed to;
  2. the EOT offset then subtracted that length from a tail that never contained it, placing the packet
     one slot early - caught by the check reading addr 0x0 at byte 364 instead of 0x20.

Both found by reading the function once, which round 78 identified as the next step.

Remaining gap to the captured working stream: 368 vs 384 = 16 bytes = 4 dwords, all before the EOT.
---
 src/gallium/drivers/pvr/pvr_csb.c | 13 ++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/pvr/pvr_csb.c b/src/gallium/drivers/pvr/pvr_csb.c
index 10716acc..9a31b97d 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/pvr/pvr_csb.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/pvr/pvr_csb.c
@@ -419,12 +419,19 @@ pvr_frag_static_stream(void *stream, uint32_t stream_size, const uint64_t *pbe_w
    const uint32_t pbe_dwords = PVR_MAX_COLOR_ATTACHMENTS * ROGUE_NUM_PBESTATE_REG_WORDS * 2;
    const uint32_t filled_dwords = nr_attachments * ROGUE_NUM_PBESTATE_REG_WORDS * 2;
    const uint32_t tail_dwords = PVR_FRAG_TAIL_DWORDS(cluster_grouping);
-   const uint32_t total_dwords = PVR_FRAG_PRE_PBE_DWORDS + pbe_dwords + tail_dwords;
+   /* PVR_FRAG_TAIL_DWORDS stops at KMD_STREAM_VIEW_IDX - the offset helper returns the point where the
+    * EOT packet is PACKED, not the end of the stream - so the EOT packet's own length has to be added
+    * for the total. Omitting it made the builder return one dword less than its own macros summed to,
+    * which is what round 78 mistook for a two-number disagreement. */
+   const uint32_t total_dwords = PVR_FRAG_PRE_PBE_DWORDS + pbe_dwords + tail_dwords +
+                                 PVR_CMD_DW(CR_EVENT_PIXEL_PDS_DATA);
    const uint32_t total_bytes = PVR_DW_TO_BYTES(total_dwords);
    const uint32_t pbe_byte_off = PVR_DW_TO_BYTES(PVR_FRAG_PRE_PBE_DWORDS);
+   /* tail_dwords stops AT the EOT packet's slot (the offset helper returns where it is packed), so the
+    * packet goes immediately after the tail - subtracting the EOT length here, as the first version did,
+    * put it one packet early. */
    const uint32_t eot_byte_off = pbe_byte_off + PVR_DW_TO_BYTES(pbe_dwords) +
-                                 PVR_DW_TO_BYTES(tail_dwords -
-                                                 PVR_CMD_DW(CR_EVENT_PIXEL_PDS_DATA));
+                                 PVR_DW_TO_BYTES(tail_dwords);
    struct ROGUE_CR_EVENT_PIXEL_PDS_DATA eot = { .addr = eot_pds_offset };
    uint32_t *dw = stream;
 
